// Codex — the programs. Every named performer holds their own entries
// from the start (the entry's `about:` is the holder). The first entry
// about each is what they'd tell a stranger; the second is what has to
// be forced out of them as the games escalate. Performers share from
// their booth; the app shows the recipient exactly and only what was
// shared.

// ── Hosts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

CODEX The Clinic
  about: Clippy
  text:
    Clippy spent five years after veterinary school at a desperately
    underfunded nonprofit veterinary clinic, helping animals all day.

CODEX Saline
  about: Clippy
  text:
    The clinic was unlicensed. It was not a nonprofit. It was not a
    veterinary clinic. It was a front for everything possible, and for
    five years Clippy injected animals with saline and believed. The fake
    vet promised to pay off her student debt and disappeared. Trabolta's
    letter promised fun philanthropy party games that would help end all
    the world's problems, and that debt would no longer be relevant.

CODEX Middle Management
  about: Task Manager
  text:
    Task Manager was a middle manager in IT at Urban Outfitters. He has no
    idiosyncrasies. He manages tasks. He has never drawn attention.

CODEX Replaced By Clippy
  about: Task Manager
  text:
    Senior management let Task Manager go when they realised he could be
    replaced by an AI Clippy. Aimless, he was Trabolta's perfect pick: a
    program with no political motivation at all, who will follow
    instructions and manage tasks and never, ever cause controversy.

CODEX Sheryl Terrio
  about: Adobe Acrobat
  text:
    Adobe Acrobat was Sheryl Terrio, the world's most successful
    motivational speaker. She built a fortune on online self-mastery
    courses. She is here to be the paid bottleneck to your creativity.

CODEX The Pirated Masterclass
  about: Adobe Acrobat
  text:
    Sheryl was so motivational that anyone who saw a single clip was
    instantly motivated to reach their full potential — and never needed
    to pay her again. When the Masterclass was pirated her income went to
    zero. She is still seeking a place to prove she is a master and be
    paid for it. Trabolta offered her one. She has not been paid.

// ── The named programs ──────────────────────────────────────────────

CODEX The Attendant
  about: Recycling Bin
  text:
    Recycling Bin was a bathroom attendant, laid off in COVID and never
    rehired. He had great potential for skilled work and never believed
    he could rise above encouraging men to groom themselves better.

CODEX The Oscars Of Bathrooms
  about: Recycling Bin
  text:
    Trabolta offered him the role of pretending to be a Recycling Bin at
    a computer-themed resort. To a bathroom attendant this is the Oscars.
    He knows about Bathroom Mode. He is proud of Bathroom Mode.

CODEX Rob Cameron
  about: Microsoft Excel
  text:
    Microsoft Excel introduces himself as Rob Cameron. He is very keen
    that everyone should stay in the computer, permanently, and points out
    that nobody ages in here. Not one cell.

CODEX Randy Barkmore Sr
  about: Microsoft Excel
  text:
    Excel is Randy Barkmore Sr., the ninety-year-old former Mayor of
    Halifax. His son Randy Jr. died in the sinkhole at the Data Centre
    opening, at 4 a.m., five hours early. Randy Sr. needs more time on
    this earth to run for Mayor once more and save the family legacy.
    Trabolta promised him everlasting life in the Cloud. He is here to
    persuade every other program to remain.

CODEX Lara Lewis
  about: OpenOffice
  text:
    OpenOffice says she is Lara Lewis. She asks a lot of questions and
    answers almost none. She has incredible fact-finding skills.

CODEX Dana Anderson
  about: OpenOffice
  text:
    OpenOffice is Dana Anderson: ex-FBI, turned hacker, who regretted a
    sting on a Halifax landlord nine years ago and decided all information
    should be free. She opposed the Data Centre like everyone in Halifax
    did — and used old FBI tactics to sabotage the site, scheduled for the
    early morning before the opening. Randy Barkmore Jr. arrived at 4 a.m.
    The sabotage ran on time. She lives with it. Trabolta wants her
    investigative skills, and thinks she wants a new life.

CODEX The Paperclip Trade
  about: DraftKings
  text:
    DraftKings traded a paperclip for a quarter, put the quarter in a
    slot machine, got a dollar, and played progressive blackjack until
    they literally won Casino Nova Scotia, then gambled it against other
    casinos and won most of Atlantic Canada.

CODEX The Boardwalk Bet
  about: DraftKings
  text:
    Obsessed with Monopoly, DraftKings bet their entire casino chain on a
    block of downtown Halifax property — the Boardwalk — in a game of
    online poker. They lost. Their opponent was Trabolta, who had already
    taken the Maps And Ducks building and needed someone powerful with
    numbers on its side.

CODEX Bugdom VR
  about: Bugdom
  text:
    Bugdom worked an unhappy pet-store job and spent every night for ten
    years designing concept assets for an extremely expansive VR version
    of the old game Bugdom. They would love to live in a VR world.

CODEX The Fire Ants
  about: Bugdom
  text:
    Fire ants got loose in Bugdom's work lunchbox and crawled into the
    laptop that held the only copy of ten years of Bugdom VR. Everything
    was lost. In a catatonic panic Bugdom began writing down everything
    they had done, to rebuild it. Trabolta saw this happening and offered
    unlimited Bugdom immediately. What he wants is their relentless
    pursuit of tedious tasks.

CODEX Jeeves Is Broken
  about: Broken Ask Jeeves
  text:
    Broken Ask Jeeves was a very good search engine, once. He has one
    answer left in him and he is saving it for a program who asks the
    right question.

CODEX Never Logged Off
  about: Runescape
  text:
    Runescape has been grinding since 2004 and has never logged off. He
    sees no reason to start. He is the most content program in the house
    and the least curious about the mud room.

// ── The Antivirus ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

CODEX Norton's Oath
  about: Norton Anti-Virus
  text:
    Norton believes, sincerely, that a program's purpose is to follow
    Trabolta's directives, and that refusing is a virus not caught at the
    door. He stands at attention because someone should.

CODEX Password Manager Knows Everything
  about: Password Manager
  text:
    Password Manager holds every code in the house and notices every
    wrong guess. If you must guess, guess out of her sight.
